    "desc": "Distil this session's transcript and hand it to a fresh agent",
    "body": "# Reads the transcript of the pane you launch this from, before step 1.\n# Works out of the box only when that pane runs claude with herdr's claude\n# integration installed. Any other agent kind needs a `transcripts:` extractor\n# in .hwf/config.yaml, or the run fails preflight. See /guide#hand-your-session-to-an-agent.\nversion: v1alpha1\ntitle: Handoff\ndescription: Distil this session's transcript and hand it to a fresh agent\ninputs:\n  target: profile\n  focus:\n    type: text\n    default: \"\"\n  placement:\n    type: choice\n    description: where the fresh agent opens\n    options: [tab, beside, below]\n    default: tab\n  close_source:\n    type: choice\n    options: [keep, close]\n    default: keep\non_failure:\n  herdr: notification.show\n  params:\n    title: handoff failed\n    body: \"{{context.error.message}}\"\n    sound: request\nsteps:\n  - id: brief\n    agent: |\n      The absolute path below is a UTF-8 file containing a coding agent session\n      transcript. Read that file and distil it into a handoff prompt for a fresh\n      agent session.\n\n      Keep (signal): architectural decisions with rationale; working solutions\n      adopted; configuration choices (versions, settings, flags, env vars);\n      files created/modified with paths and why; constraints discovered;\n      productive dead ends in one sentence each; open questions; anything the\n      next session would otherwise re-discover.\n\n      Drop (noise): corrections and retries, verbose tool output, permission\n      prompts, repeated attempts.\n\n      Use this shape, omitting empty sections:\n\n      Continue the work from the previous session. Here is the context you need:\n\n      **Project**: <path>\n      **Branch**: <branch, if known>\n\n      ## Background\n      ## What was done\n      ## Decisions in effect\n      ## Current state\n      ## Open questions\n      ## Your next steps\n      1. <directive>\n\n      Never invent decisions or context not present in the transcript; note\n      unclear items as open questions.\n\n      Transcript file — read it before you write anything, because run cleanup\n      removes it when the run ends (do not ask for its contents to be pasted):\n      {{context.transcript_file}}\n\n      Write the finished handoff to .hwf/tmp/handoff.md, relative to the repo\n      root, as well as to the file you are asked to write below. That copy\n      outlives the run.\n\n      Do not print the handoff in the chat. Printing it again costs a second\n      full render for no reader. Reply with one word: Done.\n    using: \"{{inputs.target}}\"\n    timeout: 30m\n    pane:\n      open: beside\n      focus: false\n      close: success\n\n  - herdr: notification.show\n    params:\n      title: handoff ready\n      body: \"opening {{inputs.target}} in {{inputs.placement}}\"\n      sound: done\n\n  - agent: |\n      Focus: {{inputs.focus}}\n\n      {{steps.brief.response}}\n    using: \"{{inputs.target}}\"\n    background: true\n    pane:\n      open: \"{{inputs.placement}}\"\n\n  - herdr: tab.close\n    params:\n      tab_id: \"{{context.tab}}\"\n    when:\n      - '{{inputs.close_source}} == \"close\"'\n      - '{{inputs.placement}} == \"tab\"'\n    continue_on_error: true\n\n  - herdr: pane.close\n    params:\n      pane_id: \"{{context.pane}}\"\n    when:\n      - '{{inputs.close_source}} == \"close\"'\n      - '{{inputs.placement}} != \"tab\"'\n    continue_on_error: true\n",
